From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(allwinner): A733: add initial support

Based on Yixun Lan's commit f4c0b0dba78a "feat(allwinner): A733: Add
initial support" in his TF-A tree (Link below), whose message reads
"tested only with power on/off.". The platform files keep that commit's
content where it is unchanged; the comment on SUNXI_SPC_NUM_PORTS now
says where the value comes from.

Changes against that commit: A733 only; CCMU_SEC_SWITCH_REG at CCU +
0x1F00; no SUNXI_DSP_PRCM_BASE; sunxi_cpucfg_ncat3.h reduced to
CLU0_CPUn_CTRL_REG and CLU0_RVBARADDRn_L/H; SUNXI_GICR_BASE instead of
SUNXI_GICC_BASE; CPU files and GIC-600 options in the platform's
platform.mk; SUNXI_PSCI_USE_SCPI := 0; rebased onto TF-A master.

The A733 (sun60iw2) has two Cortex-A76 and six Cortex-A55 cores in one
DynamIQ cluster, eight cores in all, and a GIC-600. Its MPIDR_EL1 has
the DynamIQ layout (SUNXI_NEW_MPIDR_FMT), its cores are powered through
Arm PPUs, and its GIC is driven by the generic GICv3 driver
(USE_GIC_DRIVER := 3). The SCPI PSCI path is built out, as on A133, H616
and R329: it expects an OpenRISC SCP behind the A31 msgbox, while the
A733's SCP is a RISC-V E902 (UM V1.00 5.2) behind a different msgbox (UM
6.1.6), and its SCP release would write bit 0 at SUNXI_R_CPUCFG_BASE, a
register of the CPUIDLE block that no A733 document describes. Register
locations follow the A733 User Manual V1.00: CCMU_SEC_SWITCH_REG is CCU
+ 0x1F00 (4.1.6.278; CCU + 0x0F00 is SPI0_CLK_REG on this SoC,
4.1.6.160), the per-core AArch64 reset-state bit is CLU0_CPUn_CTRL_REG
bit 0 and the reset vector CLU0_RVBARADDRn_L/H (5.1.6.6-5.1.6.9).
Allwinner's public SPL source agrees on both CCU offsets
(gitlab.com/tina5.0_aiot/lichee/brandy-2.0/spl-pub, commit 8f30b7df8531,
include/arch/sun60iw2p1/clock_autogen.h: CCMU_SEC_SWITCH_REG 0x1f00,
SPI0_CLK_REG 0x0f00). There is no DSP PRCM and no GICv2 CPU interface;
the GIC-600 redistributors start at SUNXI_GICR_BASE.
GICV3_IMPL_GIC600_MULTICHIP is not set: the A733 has one GIC-600, and
without multichip data the option changes nothing.

Link: https://github.com/dlan17/trusted-firmware-a/commit/f4c0b0dba78a2d9916154c130979992caa3f3156
Assisted-by: Claude
